generated C++ files are only created when compiledNimble is called. There will be multiple files resulting from each call, typically a .h and .cpp with a shared base name and multiple of those pairs. I only use Windows for testing but observe that it doesn't seem to clean up the temporary directories from each R session as immediately as OS X or linux.

Following on Chris' comments, for some reason R's function for deleting a directory is called "unlink" and does have a 'recursive' option (with the caveat that it "might not be supported on all platforms"), so you could use that.

Perry

