Whoops, I misinterpreted--my bad.  One of the developers likely has a better idea re. the solution, but dflat() places a lot of density on very high or low values of p after the ilogit transformation. A prior like beta.det[I]~dlogis(0, 1) [or dnorm(0, var=2)] might be more sensible. There might be some stuff with z that is also mucking things up, but I only took a quick glance.

John

