Hi everyone,

I was able to partially sort this problem out by not burning any samples. It appears as though the information I am giving the model must be very good because regardless of where it initializes, it is finding the year_age that is either correct or just barely off within 5 MCMC reps. So it is sampling correctly, but it is finding it much faster than would be expected. I am curious to if there may be something incorrect if the model get stuck on a single number rather than sampling multiple numbers over the course of the sampling.

